{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1518181-fan-work-shattered-glass-mage-the-awakening-big-ol-revamp","id":1518181,"title":"[FAN WORK] Shattered Glass - Mage: the Awakening | Big ol' Revamp!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-17T09:59:04-07:00","id":1518181,"title":"[FAN WORK] Shattered Glass - Mage: the Awakening | Big ol' Revamp!","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I'm one half of a writing duo who have been spending the past ten months working on this! It is a supplement/rework of a lot of Mage: the Awakening. Linked below, this 451 page book contains:<ul><li>3 New Watchtowers, Paths and attendant Supernal Realms (Paths Hypnotes, Kybernetes and Protarches, tied to the new-ish Realms of The Dream, Autochthonia and The Void)</li> <li>11 Traditions (mechanically made as mega-legacies), and the Congregation of Magical Traditions, an adaptation of the Traditions from Mage: the Ascension (some directly taken, some inspired)</li> <li>The Technocracy (again handled by the same super-legacy system used for the Traditions), back from Ascension.</li> <li>A completely revamped Seers of the Throne (that probably should have had a different name given how different they are...)</li> <li>Some rules for Potions, Magical Research and Familiars.</li> <li>Finally, an absolute shedload of lore for the Shattered Glass alternate setting that we are slowly but surely working on!</li> </ul>Naturally, we're not perfect, and this isn't done (we're still shopping around to commission art to replace the placeholders throughout, and working on edits based on feedback from the few readers we've already had). So please, if this sounds like your sort of thing, give it a read, and let us know what you think! <br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"https://dylshomebrew.blogspot.com/2023/07/shattered-glass-mage-awakening-and-hello.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://dylshomebrew.blogspot.com/20...and-hello.html</a><br /> <br /> (PS: If I've formatted this wrong or put it in the wrong place, please tell me, I'm still eminently new to the forums, I'm afraid)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28111-mrmarly","name":"MrMarly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T18:35:50-07:00","id":1518212,"title":"","content":"It seems odd to have Paths that have two Subtle and two Gross Arcanum as Ruling. Honestly, if I were to run this I might swap the Hypnotes' Prime for Life (because all living things sleep, and because the flesh can change into nightmares in the Dream), Kybernetes' Forces for Prime (because they create devices and items), and the Protarches' Matter for Death (because the Void is the absence of light and the end of all things.)<br /> <br /> Another thing to note is how much more powerful starting Mages will be with 9 Arcana dots. That's either a ton of versatility (2 Arcana at 2 dots, and 5 at 1 dot), or a specialization with a lot of elbow room (1 Arcana at 3 dots, and 3 at 2 dots). Mages are already fairly powerful in play, will the rest of your setting have the other splats buffed in a similar fashion?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, this seems really cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T01:15:29-07:00","id":1518219,"title":"","content":"The Arcana question is a good one, but some choices I'm more wed to than others.<br /> <br /> Hyponotes in particular - Them having two subtle is very deliberate given the rather unreal nature of the Dream (based in part on how Beasts operate in reality too, Atavisms not being true shapeshifting etc). Swapping out Prime for Life I feel would take away a little from them. When I say Dreaming think less Oneiros and more Neil Gaiman. <br /> <br /> The others though, those I can see the change in. Prime x Matter for Kybernetes in particular feels right (I'll sit down and talk with my co-author about it, since the artificers not having an easy path to artifice is an oversight...). Protarches I wouldn't give Death to. Space x Forces as was is a double Gross though. Space x Mind would be the obvious for Cosmic Horror flavoured Mages, but that just makes them Mastigos 2: Electric Boogaloo. Space x Spirit <i>potentially</i>, though that one I'm not too sure about.<br /> <br /> The 2 Gross/2 Subtle shtick was, at least initially, supposed to highlight the distinction. The Dream is a lot less than reality, and its Mages reflect that. Likewise Autochthonia basically <i>is</i> reality, just one step removed, and the Void is in a weird position (go far enough out in regular mundane space and you'll reach it, hypothetically). So they get two Gross because they're a lot <i>more</i> real. Though I will consider the changes for the Kybernetes in particular, they feel like they could go for it. Will get back to you shortly.<br /> <br /> As for the Power Levels - Yes. Everyone's buffing at point of CharGen. Mages absolutely come out a lot stronger, but the additions we're making to others (between the two of us Vampire and Werewolf are in progress rn and in brief - Werewolves get a lot more Pack related buffs due to an overhaul of Lodges, and Vampires will tend to just have more Disciplines than they used to at point of character creation). That's basically a straight result of both of us having found over years of playing that we almost always give a bunch of free experience to all our players at the start every single game anyway, so cooking it in with some fluff is a natural enough solution.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thank you a bunch for the feedback!<br /> <br /> - Dyl","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28111-mrmarly","name":"MrMarly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T13:57:57-07:00","id":1518267,"title":"","content":"Not sure what the etiquette is on double posting, <i>but</i> reading your feedback and talking with my co-author, we have decided on a couple of changes, and I thought you'd want to know (while I wrestle with the document at least!)<br /> <br /> Protarches Arcana changed from Space/Forces to Space/Time. Still a G/G pairing, we'll admit, but a lot less concrete than Forces (which was a peculiarity).<br /> <br /> Tradition Chargen rules tweaked a little. Major and Minor give 1 dot each (for 8), however, one of the two (Major unless your Path already gives you it) becomes Ruling, giving Tradition Mages 3 Ruling Arcana. Definitely big, but less muscling in on the Experience economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28111-mrmarly","name":"MrMarly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}